<TextLayout title="Marrow support" description="Help with YouTube summaries, AI providers, iCloud and optional tips in Marrow.">
  <p>Marrow turns YouTube captions into summaries and lets you ask follow-up questions with references to the video. It requires iOS or iPadOS 26 or later.</p>
  <h2>Get started</h2>
  <p>Paste a YouTube link into Marrow, or share a link from YouTube or Safari and choose Marrow. If Marrow is missing from the share sheet, enable it under More.</p>
  <p>Use Apple Intelligence on a supported device with Apple Intelligence enabled and its models downloaded. Availability depends on your device, language and region. Alternatively, choose OpenAI or Anthropic in Settings, enter your own API key and allow the provider to process your content. Provider usage is billed to your API account. A ChatGPT or Claude app subscription does not include API usage.</p>
  <h2>Missing captions or failed summaries</h2>
  <p>Marrow needs available captions. Some private, restricted or captionless videos cannot be processed. Check your connection and try a public video with captions. If a provider rejects a request, check your API key, model access, usage limits and API billing. Saved conversations remain available when generation fails.</p>
  <p>AI can make mistakes. Check important details against the original video using the cited timestamps. Chat answers can use provider web search for questions the captions do not answer. Those searches can incur additional API charges.</p>
  <h2>Your library and iCloud</h2>
  <p>Saved summaries and conversations are readable offline. New videos and cloud-provider requests need internet access. To sync your library, sign in to the same iCloud account and enable iCloud for Marrow. API keys stay in each device's Keychain, so enter them separately on each device.</p>
  <h2>Optional tips</h2>
  <p>Marrow is free. Small, medium and large tips are optional, one-time purchases through Apple. They unlock no features and do not pay for AI-provider usage. If products are unavailable, check your connection and tap Retry in Settings. For purchase or refund help, use <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com/">Apple's purchase support</a>.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Email <a href="mailto:support@schneider.kim">support@schneider.kim</a>. Include your device, iOS or iPadOS version, Marrow version and steps to reproduce the problem. Never send API keys. Avoid including private transcripts or messages unless needed for your request.</p>
  <p><a href="/marrow/privacy">Privacy policy</a></p>
</TextLayout>
